      "citation_reference": "NICE Clinical Guideline NG217, Section 1.9 (2022)",
      "chunk_content": "Ensure the patient is in a safe environment away from hazardous objects, sharp edges, and water. Cushion the head using a soft item. Time the seizure continuously. Call emergency medical services immediately if the seizure lasts longer than 5 minutes, if breathing remains compromised after the seizure stops, if a second seizure begins immediately, or if the individual has sustained an injury.",
      "risk_stage_tag": "ictal",
      "domain": "epilepsy"
